Z||000000||LT1 Chop Top||08-12-2001||05:09 PM||||I am a big fan of the "mirrors" in the trunk look for shows.  Who has done this, and how do you make em stick??  Velcro?  I wouldn't imagine that you keep them in when driving?  Anyone have pics and suggestions??<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||08-12-2001||05:18 PM||||You could get mirrored Lexan and leave them on.  I've used mirrored polystyrene for some things too...self stick, flexable.<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||08-12-2001||05:33 PM||||This item was for sale at the FOCOA event in Williamsburg, even given away as a door prize.  Not sure who was making it but it was selling for $75.00 for both pieces.  It was held on by both 3m tape and some glue/apoxy stuff.  Sorry, maybe someone who bought some will have the name of the guy who was selling it.  He had a sweet Black GT with 17" Crager rims.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||08-12-2001||05:44 PM||||Hi.. LT1, I don't know poot about the mirror question..  But , I just wanted to ask you if you were going to be able to make it to Houston for the New Year's Fiero Party???  I hope so... I would LOVE  to see your car in person..  Steve<BR>Ps.  I'll at least have the exterior finished on the Smoooth GT....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>NEW EMAIL..  Smooth_gt@k.st<BR>ADD on's Now...  Shaun's NOS Kit.. :)<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_3.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||LT1 Chop Top||08-12-2001||05:55 PM||||Thanks for the replies so far everyone.  I definitely DON'T want permnant mirrors in the trunk.  I think bits of velcro would work well.  Anyone have pics??<P>Smooooth, I am not sure about the Houston New Year's Eve, have any details?<P>I will however, have both of my cars entered in a Pontiac hosted open show here in San Antonio on Sunday Sept. 19 at Rolling Oaks Mall.  This is in N San Antonio near I-35 (easy access for Austinites!)  We had 10 or so Fiero's show up to represent out club.  This year we hope to have 20.  Here is a pic of the show from last year.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pontshow.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||CoolBlue87GT||08-12-2001||06:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by qwikgta:<BR><B>This item was for sale at the FOCOA event in Williamsburg,was selling for $75.00 for both pieces. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I was with Ron Hale, he bought some also, his email address is tellron@tampabay.rr.com <P>Give him a buzz, he can fill you in on the product.  It looked to be stainless steel, and was polished on one side.  The 3M tape was used, not sure if any glue was used.||||reg||6
Z||000006||tellron||08-12-2001||08:20 PM||||The person to contact is Chris Berry. He sells the stainless steel panels for $75.00. You can get them for GT or Coupe. Chris recommends silconing the panels along with 3m double sided tape. They look awesome. His email address is CBTAZ1@AOL.com Tell him Ron Hale sent ya!<P>It will definitely help putting the .com at the end. Sorry!<p>[This message has been edited by tellron (edited 08-13-2001).]||||reg||6
